# Cline Rules for Circles Documentation Project

## Project Patterns

### Documentation Structure
- All documentation follows GitBook format
- Each section has a clear README.md
- Navigation is hierarchical and intuitive
- Code examples are provided where relevant

### File Organization
- Documentation is organized by topic
- SDK reference is separate from tutorials
- Avatar types have dedicated sections
- Examples are practical and complete

### Content Style
- Technical accuracy is paramount
- Examples are concise but complete
- Step-by-step guides are preferred
- Code snippets include comments

## Implementation Patterns

### SDK Documentation
- Methods are fully documented with parameters and return types
- Examples show common use cases
- Error handling is explicitly covered
- Type definitions are included

### Tutorial Structure
- Start with setup requirements
- Include complete code examples
- Show expected outcomes
- Include troubleshooting tips

## Project Intelligence

### Critical Paths
- SDK setup and initialization
- Avatar creation and management
- Trust connection handling
- Token operations

### Known Challenges
- Complex trust network concepts
- Token transfer mechanics
- Avatar type distinctions
- Integration patterns

### User Preferences
- Clear, concise documentation
- Practical, runnable examples
- Step-by-step tutorials
- Complete API reference

## Tool Usage

### Documentation Tools
- GitBook for content hosting
- Markdown for content writing
- TypeScript for code examples
- Git for version control

### Development Flow
- Review existing docs before changes
- Update related sections together
- Include practical examples
- Test code snippets

## Evolution Notes

### Documentation Growth
- Started with core concepts
- Expanded to detailed guides
- Added comprehensive examples
- Included best practices

### Pattern Development
- Identified common implementation needs
- Developed standard examples
- Created reusable patterns
- Established best practices

## Learning Points

### Key Insights
- Avatar system is central to all operations
- Trust connections are fundamental
- Token mechanics require clear explanation
- Examples are crucial for understanding

### Important Concepts
- Personal vs Group currencies
- Trust-based transfers
- Continuous minting
- Demurrage system
